{"type":"message","id":"552af7ba","parentId":"cf66be4b","timestamp":"2026-04-02T09:20:22.972Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"No config file exists yet. The issue is that:1. There's no API key configured\n2. The login flow (OAuth) requires a browser which isn't available in this terminal session\n\nLet me think about options:\n1. Try to use `claude login` with some sort of token-based approach\n2. Check if there's a way to set up with ANTHROPIC_API_KEY directly\n3. Maybe the user needs to run `claude` or `claude login` in their own terminal first to authenticate\n\nActually, looking at the error again - \"ERR_BAD_REQUEST\" when trying to connect to api.anthropic.com. This suggests that the request IS being made but failing. If no API key is configured, it might be returning this error.\n\nLet me check if there's a way to configure an API key manually, or if the user needs to do the initial login in a browser.\n\nActually, I should inform the user that they need to do the initial login themselves, since it requires browser authentication. Let me explain this clearly.","thinkingSignature":"185004a8b3584f8ffb2a424a4f146eb1070f6fba0336beceb50991d34affa1ec"},{"type":"text","text":"发现问题了 — Claude Code 首次使用需要通过浏览器登录认证（OAuth），这个环境里没有浏览器支持。\n\n**你需要在自己的终端里操作一次：**\n\n```bash\nclaude login\n```\n\n这会打开浏览器让你授权。授权完成后，以后在这个终端里就可以直接用 `claude` 了。\n\n或者，如果你有 `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`，也可以直接设置环境变量：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_56f6vavgzcje_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"$env:ANTHROPIC_API_KEY = \"your-api-key-here\"; claude --version"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":5086,"output":339,"cacheRead":32834,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":38259,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1775121610675,"responseId":"061d67cb9dd097c8529ec434b0f2fee2"}}
